{"content_hash": "906d89a16e019b26", "version_id": 453, "article_id": 46, "level_code": "en_b1", "lang": "en", "level": 3, "level_label": "B1 中级", "title": "Panama hit by powerful 7.7 earthquake, buildings damaged", "title_zh": "巴拿马遭7.7级强震，多栋建筑受损", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c620r39zdp9wo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677233860259-ce1a8e0f8498?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cG93ZXJmdWwlMjBtYWduaXR1ZGUlMjBlYXJ0aHF1YWtlfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ2NTJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Çağlar Oskay on Unsplash", "author": "Çağlar Oskay", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@oskaycaglar?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-car-is-parked-in-front-of-a-destroyed-building-mmLtohu4qmE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(73, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(111, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "69c1918b4164"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 155, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "A powerful earthquake struck Panama on Friday afternoon. It damaged buildings and shook a wide area, but no deaths have been reported yet.", "lead_zh": "周五下午，巴拿马发生强烈地震。地震导致建筑物受损，大片地区有震感，但目前尚无人员死亡报告。", "preview": "The magnitude 7.7 earthquake hit just before 3pm local time on Friday. Its epicentre was about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in sout", "preview_zh": "这次7.7级地震发生在当地时间周五下午快到3点时。震中位于巴拿马中南部小镇皮塔洛萨阿里巴附近，距离约10公里。据美国地质调查局称，约460万人感受到了震动。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 443, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/46/en_b1.mp3", "duration": 69.263, "size_bytes": 419328, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 186, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/453.json", "paragraphs": ["The magnitude 7.7 earthquake hit just before 3pm local time on Friday. Its epicentre was about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama. About 4.6 million people felt the shaking, according to the US Geological Survey.", "Videos online show collapsed buildings in Penonomé and Soná. One side of a cathedral in Penonomé fell down, and a local hotel almost completely collapsed. However, no casualties have been reported so far.", "Ricardo Brown, 74, lives in Herrera province. He told Reuters that several homes were damaged in his neighbourhood. 'We're scared. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,' he said. Many people in Panama City also ran outside.", "The quake was only 12km deep, so the shaking was stronger on the surface. Several large aftershocks followed. Tsunami warnings were issued for 11 nearby countries, but the US later said there was no threat. The Panama Canal was not affected."], "paragraphs_zh": ["这次7.7级地震发生在当地时间周五下午快到3点时。震中位于巴拿马中南部小镇皮塔洛萨阿里巴附近，距离约10公里。据美国地质调查局称，约460万人感受到了震动。", "网上的视频显示，佩诺诺梅和索纳有建筑物倒塌。佩诺诺梅一座大教堂的一侧坍塌，当地一家酒店几乎完全倒塌。不过，目前尚无人员伤亡报告。", "74岁的里卡多·布朗住在埃雷拉省。他告诉路透社，他所在街区有几处房屋受损。他说：“我们很害怕。房子里只有我们两个老人。房子已经裂了，我们担心它会塌下来。”巴拿马城的许多人也跑到了室外。", "这次地震深度只有12公里，因此地表震动更强烈。随后又发生了多次较大余震。最初向巴拿马周边的11个国家发布了海啸预警，但美国后来表示没有威胁。巴拿马运河未受影响。"], "body": "The magnitude 7.7 earthquake hit just before 3pm local time on Friday. Its epicentre was about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama. About 4.6 million people felt the shaking, according to the US Geological Survey.\n\nVideos online show collapsed buildings in Penonomé and Soná. One side of a cathedral in Penonomé fell down, and a local hotel almost completely collapsed. However, no casualties have been reported so far.\n\nRicardo Brown, 74, lives in Herrera province. He told Reuters that several homes were damaged in his neighbourhood. 'We're scared. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,' he said. Many people in Panama City also ran outside.\n\nThe quake was only 12km deep, so the shaking was stronger on the surface. Several large aftershocks followed. Tsunami warnings were issued for 11 nearby countries, but the US later said there was no threat. The Panama Canal was not affected.", "body_zh": "这次7.7级地震发生在当地时间周五下午快到3点时。震中位于巴拿马中南部小镇皮塔洛萨阿里巴附近，距离约10公里。据美国地质调查局称，约460万人感受到了震动。\n\n网上的视频显示，佩诺诺梅和索纳有建筑物倒塌。佩诺诺梅一座大教堂的一侧坍塌，当地一家酒店几乎完全倒塌。不过，目前尚无人员伤亡报告。\n\n74岁的里卡多·布朗住在埃雷拉省。他告诉路透社，他所在街区有几处房屋受损。他说：“我们很害怕。房子里只有我们两个老人。房子已经裂了，我们担心它会塌下来。”巴拿马城的许多人也跑到了室外。\n\n这次地震深度只有12公里，因此地表震动更强烈。随后又发生了多次较大余震。最初向巴拿马周边的11个国家发布了海啸预警，但美国后来表示没有威胁。巴拿马运河未受影响。", "text": "The magnitude 7.7 earthquake hit just before 3pm local time on Friday. Its epicentre was about 10km from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama. About 4.6 million people felt the shaking, according to the US Geological Survey. Videos online show collapsed buildings in Penonomé and Soná. One side of a cathedral in Penonomé fell down, and a local hotel almost completely collapsed. However, no casualties have been reported so far. Ricardo Brown, 74, lives in Herrera province. He told Reuters that several homes were damaged in his neighbourhood. 'We're scared. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,' he said. Many people in Panama City also ran outside. The quake was only 12km deep, so the shaking was stronger on the surface. Several large aftershocks followed. Tsunami warnings were issued for 11 nearby countries, but the US later said there was no threat. The Panama Canal was not affected.", "vocab": [{"word": "earthquake", "pos": "noun", "zh": "地震", "note": ""}, {"word": "magnitude", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震级", "note": "用于描述地震强度，如 magnitude 7.7"}, {"word": "epicentre", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震中", "note": "地震发生的地下中心点"}, {"word": "damage", "pos": "verb", "zh": "损坏", "note": "也可作名词，如 cause damage"}, {"word": "collapse", "pos": "verb", "zh": "倒塌", "note": "建筑物倒塌常用词"}, {"word": "casualty", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伤亡人员", "note": "常用复数 casualties"}, {"word": "aftershock", "pos": "noun", "zh": "余震", "note": "主震后发生的小地震"}, {"word": "tsunami", "pos": "noun", "zh": "海啸", "note": "地震引发的巨浪"}, {"word": "evacuate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "疏散", "note": "把人从危险地方转移"}, {"word": "crack", "pos": "verb", "zh": "裂开", "note": "墙壁、地面等出现裂缝"}], "title_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings", "summary_original": "Tsunami warnings are issued for neighbouring countries as videos of destruction circulate online.", "body_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings\nBy\nMichael Sheils McNamee\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nA massive magnitude 7.7 earthquake has hit Panama, damaging buildings and causing widespread shaking.\nAbout 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe tremors as a result of the quake, according to the US Geological Survey, which has said that the effects of the quake were \"likely to be widespread\".\nIt struck just before 15:00 local time (18:00 GMT) on Friday, with an epicentre about 6.2 miles (10km) from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama.\nFootage shared online appears to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná, including one of a man calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. No casualties have so far been reported.\nVerified footage shows one side of a cathedral in Penonomé collapsed due to the shaking, as well as one of its spires.\nAnother video showed a local hotel had almost completely collapsed.\nRicardo Brown, who lives in the southern Herrera province, told news agency Reuters that the earthquake had damaged several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas.\n\"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" the 74-year-old said.\nThe full extent of the damage it has caused is not yet clear, though several large aftershocks were also reported near the initial earthquake, potentially complicating the situation on the surface.\nThe quake was registered as occurring at a depth of just 12km. The shallower the earthquake, the more likely it is to have more severe effects on the surface.\nMany people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and were seen taking to the streets or sitting in nearby parks until the shaking had ceased.\nDamage in the capital appears to be limited to that caused by debris falling from roofs.\nPanama's President José Raúl Mulino said his entire government was mobilising in response to the earthquake, adding: \"What happened should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.\"\nTsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 countries neighbouring Panama, before the US Tsunami Warning System confirmed there was no threat.\nThe Panama Canal - a vital waterway linking the Atlantic and Pacific oceans - was unaffected by the earthquake, the authority that oversees marine traffic through it said.\nThe earthquake comes just three days before Panama was scheduled to hold a national evacuation drill for dealing with a major earthquake.\nIt also follows devastating earthquakes in Colombia and Venezuela earlier this year.\nRelated topics\nMexico\nEarthquakes\nChile\nPanama", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:10:50.719840", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.275, "sm": 100, "em": 275, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "magnitude", "s": 0.287, "e": 0.925, "sm": 287, "em": 924, "cs": 4, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "7.7", "s": 0.938, "e": 1.913, "sm": 937, "em": 1912, "cs": 14, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "earthquake", "s": 1.925, "e": 2.462, "sm": 1925, "em": 2462, "cs": 18, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "hit", "s": 2.475, "e": 2.725, "sm": 2475, "em": 2725, "cs": 29, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "just", "s": 2.737, "e": 3.012, "sm": 2737, "em": 3012, "cs": 33, "ce": 37, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "before", "s": 3.025